Larry and David Ellison are poised to own a portfolio of companies that would put them in the orbit of superpowers like Disney.
]]&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/27/business/media/tech-tv-movies-and-news-ellisons-on-brink-of-colossal-empire.html</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Feb 2026 08:15:50 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>For CNN, a Takeover by Paramount Means a Suddenly Uncertain Future</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/27/business/media/cnn-paramount-david-ellison.html</link><description>&lt;![CDATA[
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/02/27/multimedia/27biz-ellison-news-lhpm/27biz-ellison-news-lhpm-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg" alt="Article image"/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Mark Thompson, CNN’s chief executive, urged staff members not to “jump to conclusions” about Paramount’s offer for the network’s parent, Warner Bros. Discovery.
]]&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/27/business/media/cnn-paramount-david-ellison.html</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Feb 2026 12:38:17 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>How India Became One of the World’s Biggest Economies</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/27/business/india-economy-gdp.html</link><description>&lt;![CDATA[
