The deal will make David Zaslav, the chief executive of Warner Bros. Discovery, an even richer man.
]]&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/27/business/media/david-zaslav-warner-bros-discovery-paramount.html</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Feb 2026 13:04:06 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Iris Cantor, Philanthropist and Art Collector, Dies at 95</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/27/giving/iris-cantor-dead.html</link><description>&lt;![CDATA[
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/03/01/multimedia/27cantor-cgmb-print1/27cantor-cgmb-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg" alt="Article image"/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Iris Cantor in 2001. A former model and stockbroker, she joined the bond brokerage firm Cantor Fitzgerald in 1967 and later married the founder, B. Gerald Cantor.
]]&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/27/giving/iris-cantor-dead.html</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Feb 2026 15:04:22 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Instagram to Alert Parents to Teens’ Self-Harm Searches</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/27/technology/meta-self-harm-notifications-parents.html</link><description>&lt;![CDATA[
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/02/27/multimedia/27xp-instagram-pmtl/27xp-instagram-pmtl-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg" alt="Article image"/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
Meta, which owns Instagram, is promoting the parental alerts about searches for harmful content as it is on trial in two states over claims that its platforms are addictive and have harmed young users.
]]&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/27/technology/meta-self-harm-notifications-parents.html</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Feb 2026 17:39:28 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Justice Dept. Tries to Slow Down Legal Battle Over Tariff Refunds</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/27/business/trump-tariffs-refunds-supreme-court.html</link><description>&lt;![CDATA[
